{"id":"8abe3fbe-6b54-49d7-aa0f-35ff4f207b7a","type":"level","createdDate":"2026-06-13T22:43:35.715Z","createdBy":"chaitanya.ponnapati@codeninjas.com","lastModifiedDate":"2026-06-13T22:43:35.715Z","lastModifiedBy":"chaitanya.ponnapati@codeninjas.com","attributes":{"tags":["CREATE"],"title":"Level 1","sequence":1,"activity":{"id":"b5d695a8-7322-4648-b412-39d99b083331","type":"activity","sequence":3,"group":{"id":"205d74fb-5d1e-4c04-a5bc-6cbda23268bf","type":"solve","name":null,"sequence":10,"subgroups":[{"id":"4a4ebce4-6d17-41fa-b061-654d5a119bbf","type":"subgroup","sequence":1,"name":"solve 1","steps":[{"id":"6c0c5c08-83d9-47c8-9364-2cc77ff822fc","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">❓ Did you use the documentation for help with updating the code to make the sprite say the value of each variable?</span></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><strong>Ask the ninja:</strong></p><p>❓ What does the Player sprite “say” the values of the <strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\">levelNum</strong> and <strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\">levelStarted</strong> variables are at the beginning of the project?</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p>Set <strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\">levelNum</strong> to <strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\">0</strong> and <strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\">levelStarted</strong> to <strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\">false</strong> under<strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\"> // project initialization</strong>.</p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/b04jypgz.a0q.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Ask the ninja:</strong></p><p>❓ What should the Player sprite “say” the value of the <strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\">levelStarted</strong> variable is, before and after the splash screen is displayed?</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\">levelStarted</strong> should be set to <strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\">false</strong> at the top of the <strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\">splashScreen</strong> function definition, and to <strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\">true</strong> inside the first <strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\">after</strong> function.</p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/m0emf32p.grz.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Ask the ninja:</strong></p><p>❓ What tilemap should be displayed each time the Player sprite overlaps the <strong>treeTile </strong>asset?</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\">levelNum</strong> should be set to 1 if its current value is 0, and to 0 if its current value is 1, inside the <strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\">onOverlapTile</strong> event.</p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/tk1mbgne.z3p.png\"></p>","instructions":"<p>Use the <strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\">sayText</strong> function to debug the code to create a working project!</p><p><br></p><p>Variables are useful for keeping track of game conditions in the project. The <strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\">sayText</strong> function allows a sprite to “say” the value of a variable, allowing you to check if it’s updating correctly throughout the project.</p><p><br></p><p>Click ▶ to test out the project. Notice the value that is displayed on the splash screen, and when the Player sprite is able to move.</p><p><br></p><p>Find the code under <strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\">// debugging code</strong> in the editor. Use the <strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\">sayText</strong> function to make the Player sprite say the value of each variable throughout the project.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Update the <strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\">levelNum</strong> and <strong class=\"ql-font-monospace\">levelStarted</strong> variables, so that the correct level number shows and the Player sprite is <em>not</em> able to move when the splash screen is displayed.</p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null}],"title":"Debugging Projects Using the sayText Function","project":{"editor":{"filters":[],"searchBar":true},"source":{"text":{"main.ts":"// project initialization\nlet levelNum = 1\nlet levelStarted = true\nlet tilemaps = [assets.tilemap`topDownTilemap`, assets.tilemap`2Dtilemap`]\nlet startingPos = [[1,1], [1,6]]\n\nlet playerSprite = sprites.create(assets.image`playerSprite`, SpriteKind.Player)\nscene.cameraFollowSprite(playerSprite)\n\nfunction callScene (sceneNum: number) {\n    tiles.setCurrentTilemap(tilemaps[sceneNum])\n    tiles.placeOnTile(playerSprite, tiles.getTileLocation(startingPos[sceneNum][0], startingPos[sceneNum][1]))\n    if (sceneNum == 0 && levelStarted) {   \n        controller.moveSprite(playerSprite)\n        playerSprite.ay = 0\n    } else if (sceneNum == 1 && levelStarted) {\n        controller.moveSprite(playerSprite, 50, 0)\n        playerSprite.ay = 250\n    } else {\n        controller.moveSprite(playerSprite, 0, 0)\n    }\n}\n\nfunction splashScreen() {\n    levelStarted = true\n    let splashScreen = sprites.create(assets.image`splashScreen`)\n    let splashText = textsprite.create(\"Level \" + (levelNum + 1), 0, 12)\n    splashText.setPosition(65, 55)\n    splashText.setMaxFontHeight(10)\n    timer.after(3000, function () {\n        sprites.destroy(splashScreen)\n        sprites.destroy(splashText)\n        levelStarted = false\n    })\n    timer.after(3000, function() {\n        callScene(levelNum)\n    })\n}\n\n// project start\nsplashScreen()\ncallScene(levelNum)\n\n// project events    \ncontroller.A.onEvent(ControllerButtonEvent.Pressed, function() {\n    if (levelNum == 1 && levelStarted) {\n        playerSprite.vy = -100\n    }\n})\n\nscene.onOverlapTile(SpriteKind.Player, assets.tile`treeTile`, function(sprite: Sprite, location: tiles.Location) {\n    if (levelNum == 0) {\n        levelNum = 0\n    } else if (levelNum == 1) {\n        levelNum = 1\n    }\n    splashScreen()\n    levelStarted = false\n    callScene(levelNum)\n})\n\n// debugging code\nforever(function () {\n    playerSprite.sayText(\":)\")\n})\n","pxt.json":"{\n    \"name\": \"BB Mini Golf Solve 3\",\n    \"description\": \"\",\n    \"dependencies\": {\n        \"device\": \"*\",\n        \"arcade-text\": \"github:microsoft/arcade-text#v1.3.0\",\n        \"Timers\": \"github:microsoft/arcade-timers#v1.1.0\"\n    },\n    \"files\": [\n        \"main.ts\",\n        \"README.md\",\n        \"assets.json\",\n        \"tilemap.g.jres\",\n        \"tilemap.g.ts\",\n        \"images.g.jres\",\n        \"images.g.ts\"\n    ],\n    \"targetVersions\": {\n        \"branch\": \"v1.12.36\",\n        \"tag\": \"v1.12.36\",\n        \"commits\": \"https://github.com/microsoft/pxt-arcade/commits/e7b91fde1aac75ec4eac478e6a2d132891a06eb9\",\n        \"target\": \"1.12.36\",\n        \"pxt\": \"8.5.49\"\n    },\n    \"preferredEditor\": \"tsprj\",\n    \"languageRestriction\": \"javascript-only\"\n}\n","readmE.md":null,"assets.json":"","main.blocks":"<xml xmlns=\"https://developers.google.com/blockly/xml\"></xml>",".simstate.json":"{}","images.g.jres":"{\n    \"image1\": {\n        \"data\": \"hwQQABAAAAAAAADA/P8PAAAAADwzu/8AALvLM8PM+/+wGzEzzMz72zsTMTPLzPzdOzMzs93du907MzOz3d3NuzszM9vN3c0MsDMz293c3QywMTPb3d3d/7ARw9vdvd3/sBvD3My93bsAO8PM3b39uwA8s8y83fy/AMy7u8z/AP8AwPz/AAAAAA==\",\n        \"mimeType\": \"image/x-mkcd-f4\",\n        \"displayName\": \"playerSprite\"\n    },\n    \"image2\": {\n        \"data\": \"\",\n        \"mimeType\": \"image/x-mkcd-f4\",\n        \"displayName\": \"splashScreen\"\n    },\n    \"*\": {\n        \"mimeType\": \"image/x-mkcd-f4\",\n        \"dataEncoding\": \"base64\",\n        \"namespace\": \"myImages\"\n    }\n}","images.g.ts":"// Auto-generated code. Do not edit.\nnamespace myImages {\n\n    helpers._registerFactory(\"image\", function(name: string) {\n        switch(helpers.stringTrim(name)) {\n            case \"image1\":\n            